  "question": {
    "text": "Water emerges from a tap vertically downwards with an initial speed of <math><mn>1.0&nbsp;</mn><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow></mrow></math>. The cross-sectional area of the tap is <math><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>–</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>. Assume that the pressure is constant throughout and that the flow is steady, the cross-sectional area of the stream <math><mn>0.15</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> below the tap is"
  },
